            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0204" n="1038" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1038"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/9730</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-24T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 24, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5427. For McFadden [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 266. Embassy’s 4710, your 329, August 8, 12 a.m. War Trade Board has been
                    informed by Italian representative on Washington <pb facs="0205" n="1039"
                        xml:id="pg1039"/> black-list committee that Italian Government not prepared
                    to participate in enemy trading license conference. British Government [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Embassy</hi>] has received cable from Foreign Office,
                    London, stating that French representative in Washington states French
                    Government prepared to agree in event certain further exceptions made. From this
                    it would appear that French Government has not as yet given full agreement.
                    Communicate with French authorities and inform us exactly of their position in
                    the matter. Impress upon them desirability of full cooperation and unity in
                    these matters. Inform us fully of exceptions which French Government desires to
                    make, giving examples. Also give your personal opinion as to desirability of
                    such exceptions and state reasons which in your opinion underlie desires of
                    French Government for these exceptions. French representative in Washington is
                    cabling his Government for full information as to their position. Important that
                    full agreement be reached between English, French, and United States
                    immediately. Pending final agreement, we will transmit to you such cases as
                    would be submitted to Paris conference. You will discuss these informally with
                    proper French authorities and proper British official in Paris. You will cable
                    result of each discussion to War Trade Board. Upon definite agreement reached
                    with French Government, formal conference will be resumed without awaiting
                    Italian participation. You will be notified.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
